WEBVTT

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.970
Enemy craft detected ahead of us too.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.160
Damn it!

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.140
What do we do now, Mister?

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.240
Mister?

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.740
Mister!

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.650
To the right! Right!

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.340
You sure that's the right gate?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.650
Just get the heck in there!

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.810
Fire!

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.150
Hokorimamire no bonnet

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:57.550
yubi de kyou o kizamu

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:01.020
Toori ame ga sugiru koro

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.860
ai no you ni kieta

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:11.100
Kokoro no naka nakusenu mono aru kara

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:17.770
Mienai tsubasa habatakase

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:24.470
Koredemo katto fuku kaze ni mukaiuchi

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:31.720
Yuruginai kimochi de tachimukatteku no sa, go!

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:38.630
Sunabokori mau yakusoku no basho e

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:44.630
Oretachi wa hashiritsuzukete yuku

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.760
Konya koso

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.270
Koete yaru

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:59.090
Ano saki made

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.050
One, two, three...

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.150
Katana!

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.760
This is bad, man.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.420
We're friggin out of anesthetics.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.190
What did you say?

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.360
If we don't get these bullets out
of him quick, he's screwed!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.020
Do it...

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:50.860
Huh?

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.030
Do it without the anesthetic.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.840
But...

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.470
Look, just do it.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.440
Okay...

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.280
Here goes, Boss.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.630
Episode 7   Marciano, the Traitor

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.060
So it's over then.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.190
It's not over.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.970
Isn't it?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.530
I've got the calculation results.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.200
Going from this point...

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.620
Right about the time we touch down
on Graceland...

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.660
It goes ka-boom.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.470
We can't go to Graceland;

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.800
the man with the plan is down and out;

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.340
we've got our hands tied behind our
backs and no way to turn.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.770
Well, Son, to put it plainly, that means it's all over.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.010
You almost sound happy about it.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.880
Aw, I wouldn't say that.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.910
If this is how it's gonna be,

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.940
we'll just have to go back to Big Pink,
and get to Graceland from there.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.960
The exit gate probably won't be useable
after that explosion earlier,

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.650
but the entrance side hasn't been
destroyed, now has it?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.690
You don't learn, do you?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.730
Big Pink must be strengthening its
defenses right about now.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:32.070
What the heck are we going to accomplish
by going back there?

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.330
Shut the hell up!

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.400
We're moths about to fly right into the flame!

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.910
Stop your damn bitching!

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.540
Let's go, Katana!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.940
Right!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.920
<i>Gate 5 has been severely damaged.</i>

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.550
<i>Give me a damage report.</i>

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.260
<i>System output percentage currently at 64%.</i>

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:58.290
<i>Notify all space gate stations of cruise restrictions.</i>

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:02.860
It looks like it will be a while before 
we can use this gate to go after Mister.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.800
I wonder if Mister and his gang made
it through the gate all right?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.770
I'm confirming their progress now.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:11.030
It sounds like the damage to that
gate is pretty bad though.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.280
Yes. Yes.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:19.180
One mid-sized craft of unknown affiliation took off.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:20.380
Yes.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.210
Thank you very much.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.240
Angelica!

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:28.550
The Coyote survived.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:42.930
Pretty Red return gate's warp space stream
reversal operation complete!

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.940
We can launch a direct attack on Pretty Red!

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:56.080
Energy charge at 99.9% output.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.880
We can fire at full power.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:05:59.710
Very well.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.550
Fire!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.200
<i>Presently, all flights to and from
Pretty Red have been halted.</i>

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:29.410
<i>I repeat: Presently, all flights to and from Pretty Red have been halted.</i>

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:25.450
All right.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:30.620
We'll go in just like this and blow right past 
the administration bureau, gate and everything!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.950
<i>I repeat: Presently, all flights...</i>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.870
It's all you, man.


00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:05.250
Mister will now no longer be able to return.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:18.460
This ship will now go through the
Graceland gate and on to Graceland!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.390
Instruct Big Pink's control tower to open the gate.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.340
Once all the soldiers are rounded up,

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.900
we will head toward the Graceland gate and depart!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.980
What the hell?!

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.850
Marciano's work.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.480
Only that woman would do something
this overboard.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.840
That woman again?!

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.490
Goddamn!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.980
So it's over at last.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.830
Oh, have I offended you?

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:48.260
Son of a bitch...

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.100
Why don't you just give in and admit that it's over?

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:56.740
Shut the hell up.
I'm telling you it ain't over, pal.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.070
What's the matter?

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:00.130
Looks like you're having some fun there.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.010
Mister?!

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.240
Let me in on this too.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.750
You sure you're all right?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.410
Yeah!

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.050
Aren't you better off resting?

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.320
Even if you push yourself,
by the time we make it to Graceland,

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:18.560
it sounds like the photonic bomb will have
reduced the treasure to space dust.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.290
Is that right?

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:21.530
Yeah...

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:23.700
I calculated that if we can't use a space gate,

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:30.040
then we'll reach Graceland right around the moment
that they drop the photonic bomb on it.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:31.440
So there you go.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.610
Well, you just give up now and go rest
and recover as much as you like.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.710
Why don't I...

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.780
What are you talking about?

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.910
This game's just getting started.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:42.480
Mister!

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.280
Mister!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.990
You got some kinda plan?

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.650
My plan?

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.530
I don't have a plan.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:56.120
But that doesn't mean our odds
have dropped to zero.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.140
For one thing, it's still possible the war could end,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.640
or that the bomb could be screwed up
somehow and not explode,

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:09.870
or that its convoy could end up arriving
later than planned.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.770
But you might as well pray to God
for any of that to happen!

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:16.180
Not at all.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:19.720
Before Bruce cracked Gigabanks,

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.350
it's not like he started off with any
proof that it could be done.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.760
You gotta start by giving it a shot.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.990
That's what he must have done.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.630
That's the kind of guy Bruce was.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.670
We've got a big problem to deal with,
that's for sure,

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:42.610
but we've also got a lot of things
going for us that Bruce didn't.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:46.450
Bruce had to start out by
researching a bunch of things,

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:49.350
but we were able to see the results
through his eyes.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:54.560
On the other hand, we have
the burden of a time limit.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:59.390
Bruce couldn't afford to let anyone else
find out about his plan,

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.500
but we don't have that kind of restraint.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.130
On the other hand, we do have the
likes of Marciano to deal with.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.070
And we've got an ally too.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.460
You really are an optimist, Boss.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:15.440
Hey, you're probably thinking we'll
figure something out too. Right?

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:22.350
It's just I wouldn't call it the
same thing in your case.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:23.990
Optimistic is one thing, but...

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.510
Happy-go-lucky!

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.380
There you go.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.100
Gates 5 and 2 have sustained severe damage!

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.120
Give me a damage report on
each of the affected areas.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.320
What should we do, Angelica?

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.860
Are you all right?

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.500
You are, aren't you?

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:48.300
Angelica?

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:54.880
Let's go to Graceland.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.520
As long as whatever Mister is after is on Graceland,

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.490
I'm sure he'll come.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.720
It's Mister we're talking about, so I'm certain.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.300
The old guy can sure take a lot of abuse.

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:14.960
That's the truth.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:21.780
All right then, shall we be off again?

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.010
I dunno how this is going to tum out, but...

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.280
Look out, Graceland, here we come!

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:47.740
Move your fingers one by one,
starting with your index finger.

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:48.670
Yes, sir.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.370
Looks good.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:55.070
Okay then, why don't we try a little typing test?

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:57.670
Now type what you see here.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.220
Does anything feel off?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:08.690
No, nothing.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.660
Very good, very good indeed.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.730
Say, Master Nilson?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.930
What is it?

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:20.990
I ruined those clothes you gave me
in our last battle.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.160
Me too. I'm sorry.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:25.810
Is that all?

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.140
It's no trouble at all.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:30.700
It means I'll have the pleasure of
giving you gifts once again.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.280
When this is all over, let's all go shopping again.

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:37.510
Yes, sir.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:48.730
Bruce, eh?

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:49.800
Yeah...

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.600
How did the maintenance on my daughters go?

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.470
Without a hitch.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.470
Ah, that's good.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:13:01.280
Bruce's legacy does not strike me as
something you will easily obtain.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:05.340
Small wonder that he was known as the Pirate King.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.680
He was a fool of a man.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.320
Even if you go to the trouble of stealing a fortune,

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.950
dying renders it all meaningless.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.750
I believe you're the one who did it.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.990
Do you regret it?

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:23.120
Regret? How absurd!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:29.540
Killing him left things unsettled.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:31.370
That's all.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:35.040
And that is why I am going to Graceland.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:39.440
Unsettled? With whom did you
have a score to settle?

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:44.140
Was it with Bruce? Or do you mean
settling matters with yourself?

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.420
It seems we've arrived.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:50.580
It's about time I went up to the bridge.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:58.900
She should be more honest with herself.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:04.770
A number of craft sighted in the
vicinity of the Graceland gate.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.100
Distance, 2,000.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:09.540
One battleship-class vessel,
twelve cruiser-class vessels.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:12.410
Crosschecking the battleship class vessel...

00:14:13.010 --> 00:14:14.140
It's an El Dorado-class.

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:16.820
I believe it is one of Hunter's ships.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.390
Hunter?

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.890
Is it a Guild fleet?

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:22.860
We have an incoming call from Hunter Bennet.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:24.390
Shall I put it through?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.650
What seems to be the problem?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.530
Mother, we are receiving a call from Hunter Bennet.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:35.070
How shall I proceed?

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:37.970
What? Hunter Bennet?

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:42.200
Is the Guild's foremost execution squad
making their appearance?

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:46.350
Hunter's fleet appears to be lying
in ambush outside the gate.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.620
April...

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:48.840
Yes?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.520
We now have one more diversion to enjoy,
wouldn't you say?

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:54.880
Yes.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.840
<i>It has been quite some time, Madame.</i>

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.540
Quite some time, Hunter.

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.340
My, you look well.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:16.410
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:20.640
<i>I am delighted that you seem as
ostentatious as ever in your pursuits.</i>

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:26.650
<i>I was quite taken aback when I heard of the incident
on Big Pink between you and the blasted Coyotes.</i>

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.190
Oh, were you?

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:33.820
I trust that you, Madame, wise as you are,
will be able to deduce why I am here.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:40.960
My fleet has been given orders to capture you or
to dispose of you if capture is not possible.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:45.170
However, I see no reason for fellow
Guild members to fight each other.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.340
Fellow Guild members...

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:51.240
<i>What would you say to returning with me
and facing a Guild tribunal?</i>

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:56.950
<i>You no doubt know the fate of those who fly the flag
of rebellion against the Guild, don't you, Madame?</i>

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.690
You've certainly climbed through
the ranks, haven't you?

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:01.750
<i>Eh?</i>

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:04.360
<i>Ah, yes, I've been fortunate.</i>

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.060
Is your wife doing well?

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.430
<i>Uh, yes.</i>

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:10.530
I hear you had a child just last year.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.870
<i>Yes...</i>

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.400
Are you sure about this?

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.560
<i>Huh?</i>

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:20.970
My soldiers may be paying your home
a visit right about now.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.720
<i>Very well.</i>

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.550
<i>Then that is your answer, Madame?</i>

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.030
Everyone, this is Marciano.

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:44.870
This ship shall now break through the
enemy fleet spread out ahead,

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:46.770
and continue on toward Graceland.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:52.100
We of the Criminal Guild have come here
to exist as a true "guild."

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:54.480
We must not become like the current Guild,

00:16:54.480 --> 00:16:57.240
which has declined so far that it now resembles
little more than a corporation.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:02.820
The spirit of the Guild lives on only
in us of the Criminal Guild.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:07.960
Let us teach those who have sat so comfortably
under the auspices of the Guild...

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.820
what true power is!

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.070
They say it's Hunter!

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:22.040
Oh, my, it really has been so long.

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:27.270
Moving an entire fleet against
 a single target? So typical.{Is it typical to move an entire fleet
against a single target?}

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:31.310
Three small-sized craft appear to have
launched from Marciano's vessel.

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:35.680
Send out all Guild Skies.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.670
All ships maintain formation
and advance at low speed.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:48.520
I truly appreciate your ever youthful attitude.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.960
However, striking out against a great fleet such as
this with but a single ship is beyond recklessness.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.700
Seriously.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.170
I actually pity you.

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.570
Well, I guess I'll go first.

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:08.880
No fair!

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:27.060
We've finally made it to the Graceland gate.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.440
This is just the start.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:32.110
You're so tough, Angelica.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.240
And I'm even six years younger than you!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.370
I mean, look at how glossy my skin is and all!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.880
I guess it's the obsession with Mister
that makes all the difference, huh?

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:46.490
The battle zone is expanding.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:49.080
Prepare to sustain damage from debris.

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.590
I'm in charge here. The name is Ted Roy.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:54.030
I'm Inspector Angelica Burns.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.930
I apologize for interrupting at
such an inopportune time.

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:59.770
I've received notification from
the Federal Offices

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:02.000
that you are in pursuit of Mister.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:02.940
Yes.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:06.270
Do you truly intend to go to Graceland?

00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:07.870
Yes.

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.340
I see...

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.110
We shall return your ship,

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:17.020
but with circumstances as they are,
I must ask that you pilot it on your own.

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:18.780
I understand.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.500
That's eight.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.010
Eight for me too!

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.410
You're not winning this one!

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:51.380
What are Guild ships doing
fighting each other here?!

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.850
Five cruisers sunk,
three have sustained serious damage.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:22.940
Guild Skies are almost completely annihilated!

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:25.780
Wh..who the hell are these people?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.080
One enemy fighter approaching at high speed!

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.260
Fire! Fire!

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.420
Don't let it near us!

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:50.640
You ought to have worried more
about your own fate.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:14.420
Graceland...

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:24.980
If we do a swing-by using the Logos and Thanatos
systems, which are en route...

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:32.820
Plus, we put the engines in overboost
to gain even more speed...

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:36.580
Well?

00:21:36.720 --> 00:21:40.790
If I plug all the variables in,
it tells me we save half a day and change.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.590
That'll work.

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:45.560
Looks to me like we'll make it.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:47.500
Mister!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.270
You all right now?

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.610
You think I can just lie there
on my back doing nothing?

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:54.770
I guess you guys have decided what to do?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.310
Yeah...

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:59.500
Our only choice is to delay the
dropping of the photonic bomb.

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:04.050
None of that!

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.020
You're wounded. Alcohol is off-limits!

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.650
Oh, she's good!

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:20.100
Bruce, the man you approved of
is finally taking this seriously.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:23.100
You're probably watching it all yourself
from somewhere in space.

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:25.470
Let's both see this through to the end.

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:43.960
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru</i>

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:54.560
<i>shizuku doko kara kuru no</i>

00:22:54.560 --> 00:23:00.730
<i>Oshiete...</i>

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:05.360
<i>Makimodosenai </i>

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:11.820
<i>jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:19.920
<i>munagura tsukanda</i>

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:23.540
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae</i>

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:27.130
<i>Usuragu kioku ni </i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:33.850
<i>teikou suru keredo</i>

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:37.720
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru</i>

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:44.110
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de</i>

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:53.030
<i>tatta hitotsu shinjirareru</i>

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:58.790
<i>Koe o karasete naita</i>

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:02.210
<i>Koko e kite</i>

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:05.670
<i>Soba ni ite</i>

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:10.100
<i>Nee</i>
